# Dagric OS — graphics drivers in plain words.
# driver | plain name | note appended to the line (may be empty)
#
# KEEP THE NOTE UNDER 62 CHARACTERS. It is printed verbatim at an indent of
# 14, and the report is written to sit inside a 78-column window. A longer
# note is not truncated — it just pushes that one line off the right-hand
# edge, which is exactly the sort of small ugliness that makes a diagnostic
# look untrustworthy to the person relying on it.

i915        | Intel built-in graphics        | Supported out of the box. Nothing to install.
xe          | Intel Arc / newer graphics     | Nothing to install.
amdgpu      | AMD graphics                   | AMD write this driver themselves. Nothing to install.
radeon      | AMD graphics (older card)      | Nothing to install.
nouveau     | NVIDIA card, community driver  | It works, but it is slow for games and 3D. See below.
nvidia      | NVIDIA card, official driver   | Already installed and in use.
nvidia_drm  | NVIDIA card, official driver   | Already installed and in use.

# Virtual and server display chips. Named so a report from a VM or a
# refurbished server does not read as a fault.
virtio_gpu  | virtual display (VM)           |
virtio-pci  | virtual display (VM)           |
vmwgfx      | VMware virtual display         |
qxl         | virtual display (VM)           |
bochs       | virtual display (VM)           |
bochs-drm   | virtual display (VM)           |
hyperv_drm  | Hyper-V virtual display        |
ast         | ASPEED server display chip     |
mgag200     | Matrox server display chip     |
simpledrm   | basic display, no real driver  | The screen works, but with no acceleration. Usually means the proper driver did not load.
